The effect of age on responses to HUD warnings
Older drivers responded to HUD warnings significantly slower than younger drivers (p=0.0008, 826 vs. 1153 ms , a 40 percent dif ference). The interaction between row and age, and column and age were both significant (p=0.04 for both) with older drivers responding relatively more slowly to locations on the right (Figure 4) and showing greater  differences between rows.
